<title>USA: Corn Refiners leader Claassen dies in plane crash.</title>
<headline>Corn Refiners leader Claassen dies in plane crash.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The president of the Corn Refiners Association, Terry Claassen, and his son died in an airplane accident, the trade group said Thursday.</p>
<p>In a statement, the group said Claassen, 48, and son Benjamin, 18, died Tuesday in the crash of a four-seater plane that Claassen was piloting.</p>
<p>Claassen was president and treasurer of the trade group since late 1990. During his career, he was a congressional staff worker, held senior posts at the Commodity Futures Trading Commission and worked for a St Louis law firm.</p>
<p>Survivors include his wife, Rosemary, and son, Nicholas.</p>
